			Let $\ell = (\sigma,g)$ and $\ell' = (\sigma',g')$ be elements of $\mathbb{L}$ such that $\operatorname{dom}(g)\subseteq \operatorname{dom}(g')$. Say that $\operatorname{dom}(g) = \bar{b}$, $g(\bar{b}) = \bar{x}$, and $g'(\bar{b}) = \bar{y}$. 
			Then $\ell\equiv_k\ell'$ if $(\sigma,\bar{x})\equiv_k (\sigma',\bar{y})$.

