			\begin{enumerate}

				\item For $k = n-1$ being \emph{reasonable} means that $\ell^n_i\subseteq\ell^{n-1}_j$ for $m_i\leq j\leq m$.  In addition, $\ell^n_p\subseteq u^n_{p+1}$, and if $\ell^n_i = (\sigma,g)$ and $u^n_{i+1} = (\tau,h,\bar{v})$, then $\operatorname{dom}(g) = \operatorname{dom}(h)$.

